ted Casket","Simon Aldicott","West Commonlands","A Tortured Revenant","Revenant Ash","Valeron Dushire","Kaladim"],"dialogue":[{"npc":"Diggs Duggun","text":"ail, dere! Ain'tcha a sight fer me sore eyes! I knows dat we're strangers an' all, but might I ask a [boon] of ye?"},{"npc":"Diggs Duggun","text":"Well, me pickaxe is blunted awfully bad and me ale supplies are dangerously low. If'n ye would be kind enough t' get me a new pick and a couple o' bottles o' dwarven ale, I would be f'rever in yer debt."},{"npc":"Diggs Duggun drinks one of the ales and burps loudly then","text":"By Brell's Beard! Yer a lifesaver, ya are! 'ere, take dis bone I've found 'ere in dis maze. Looks human ta me and I'm thinkin that a proper burial is in order. Freeport's the closest place dat has one o Marr's temples. I'm thinkin dis was one o' his Holy Knights by da look o' da tattered tunic I found it wrapped in. I'm thinkin Valeron might be havin an interest in it."},{"npc":"Valeron Dushire","text":"I am Sir Valeron Dushire, leader of the order of the Knights of Truth. If your soul shines with purity and strength, I urge you to join our order. The might of Mithaniel Marr stands behind all who join. Soon that might will help us free this city from the tyranny of the [Freeport Militia]."},{"npc":"Valeron Dushire","text":"Hail, adventurer! I... what's this? Where did you get this? Never mind.. I.. I never thought we would find [him]!"},{"npc":"Valeron Dushire","text":"According to this crest on the tunic, you have recovered one of the bones of a lost Paladin [Hero]."},{"npc":"Valeron Dushire","text":"His name has been long lost but his legend lives on in every young knight who aspires to continue his fight. He attempted to quell an evil that resided within Kithicor, perverting nature itself. Much to his relief, it was an earthly foe he fought against and not a denizen summoned from the planes of evil. Then, suddenly, he was surrounded by dozens of dark elves. He was captured and taken to the Dead to be experimented upon and had his soul twisted by vile necromantic magics. Then the Tier'Dal cast his remains to the winds. Where they landed, no one knew, until now. You have found one of his bones. I hereby charge you with a Holy Quest to bring this Hero's bones back for a burial with honors. Do you [accept], knight?"},{"npc":"Valeron Dushire","text":"Good! I knew you would. It is one of the highest honors one can receive. Your quest will not be easy for I know not where his other bones lay. A spy of ours within Neriak was able to surmise that six of his bones along with his sword and shield were scattered throughout Norrath. You must search far and wide to find the remaining pieces, as you already have one.. Do not give up. It is now your sacred duty. Once you have retrieved all eight pieces, come back to me and inform me that you [have all the bones]."},{"npc":"Valeron Dushire","text":"Excellent! You are indeed worthy to bear the title of Holy Knight! Now, about the coffin. I have spoken with Ping Fuzzlecutter, outside the western gates. Ask him about the coffin and once it is made, bring it to Simon Aldicott of Marr. I shall have Simon meet you by the lake in the Commonlands after Ping gives you the coffin."},{"npc":"Simon Aldicott","text":"Hail and well met, ______. I am Simon Aldicott, a cleric in the service of Mithaniel Marr. I've been sent here to prepare a [funeral service] for one of our lost to join Marr in his kingdom."},{"npc":"Simon Aldicott","text":"Are you the brave knight whom Valeron sent to meet me here? If so, please place the remains in the coffin and seal it. Then hand me the coffin so that we may bless it in the waters of this lake."},{"npc":"Simon Aldicott","text":"Thank you Knight. With this task accomplished, I shall reward you with this scroll. It is an ancient spell that only the holiest of knights may cast. Remember your duty!"},{"npc":"Ping Fuzzlecutter smiles broadly as he rifles through the bag, then looks up at you and","text":"Bout time! Here is the coffin as promised."},{"npc":"A Tortured Revenant's corpse","text":"At last I can rest.."}],"fetchedAt":"2026-10-07T07:01:17.906Z","outOfEra":false}
